*> Linear mixed models: a random intercept on the penguins data, then a random intercept
*> and slope on simulated multi-school data, with BLUPs and predictions.
*> The simulation uses FUNCTION RANDOM, so its numbers differ from other languages' runs.
*> Run with `just run-cobol TARGET=lmm_ex`.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. LMM-EX.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge.cpy".

78 N-SCHOOLS VALUE 30.
01 TRUE-INTERCEPT USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 60.0.
01 TRUE-SLOPE     USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 3.0.

*> Each school's deviation from the population intercept and slope.
01 SCHOOL-EFFECTS.
   05 SCHOOL-EFFECT OCCURS 30.
      10 SCHOOL-INTERCEPT USAGE COMP-2.
      10 SCHOOL-SLOPE     USAGE COMP-2.
*> The simulated students: up to 30 schools x 35 students.
01 STUDENTS.
   05 SCHOOL-COL      USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 1050.
   05 STUDY-HOURS-COL USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 1050.
   05 SCORE-COL       USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 1050.
01 N-STUDENTS-TOTAL USAGE BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.

01 PENGUINS        USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 SPECIES-MODEL   USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 DF              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 MODEL           USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 GROUP-LABELS    USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 RANDOM-EFFECTS  USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 NEWDATA         USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 PREDICTION      USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 S               USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 J               USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 I               USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 N-STUDENTS      USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 GROUP-INDEX     USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 HOURS           USAGE COMP-2.
01 NOISE           USAGE COMP-2.
01 GAUSS-VALUE     USAGE COMP-2.
01 U1              USAGE COMP-2.
01 U2              USAGE COMP-2.
01 INTERCEPT-SHIFT USAGE COMP-2.
01 SLOPE-SHIFT     USAGE COMP-2.
01 COLUMN-NAME     PIC X(32).

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    DISPLAY "=================== Random intercept on a real dataset (penguins) ==================="
    CALL "dm_data_frame_penguins" USING DM-DATA-FRAME-PENGUINS DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-DATA-FRAME-PENGUINS-RESULT TO PENGUINS
    MOVE PENGUINS TO DM-LMM-NEW-DATA
    MOVE "body_mass_g ~ flipper_length_mm + bill_length_mm + (1 | species)" TO DM-LMM-NEW-FORMULA
    CALL "dm_lmm_new" USING DM-LMM-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-LMM-NEW-RESULT TO SPECIES-MODEL
    MOVE SPECIES-MODEL TO DM-LMM-PRINT-SUMMARY-SELF
    CALL "dm_lmm_print_summary" USING DM-LMM-PRINT-SUMMARY DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK

    DISPLAY " "
    DISPLAY "=================== Random intercept + slope on a simulated multi-school dataset ==================="
    *> 30 schools, ~25 students each: score depends on study_hours, but both the baseline
    *> score and the return on an extra hour of study vary by school -- the textbook case
    *> for a random-intercept-and-slope model.
    MOVE FUNCTION RANDOM(2024) TO U1
    PERFORM VARYING S FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL S > N-SCHOOLS
        PERFORM GAUSS
        COMPUTE SCHOOL-INTERCEPT(S) = GAUSS-VALUE * 6.0
        PERFORM GAUSS
        COMPUTE SCHOOL-SLOPE(S) = GAUSS-VALUE * 1.2
    END-PERFORM
    PERFORM VARYING S FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL S > N-SCHOOLS
        *> 15 to 35 students.
        COMPUTE N-STUDENTS = 15 + FUNCTION INTEGER(FUNCTION RANDOM * 21)
        PERFORM N-STUDENTS TIMES
            COMPUTE HOURS = FUNCTION RANDOM * 10.0
            PERFORM GAUSS
            COMPUTE NOISE = GAUSS-VALUE * 4.0
            ADD 1 TO N-STUDENTS-TOTAL
            COMPUTE SCHOOL-COL(N-STUDENTS-TOTAL) = S - 1
            MOVE HOURS TO STUDY-HOURS-COL(N-STUDENTS-TOTAL)
            COMPUTE SCORE-COL(N-STUDENTS-TOTAL) = TRUE-INTERCEPT + SCHOOL-INTERCEPT(S)
                + (TRUE-SLOPE + SCHOOL-SLOPE(S)) * HOURS + NOISE
        END-PERFORM
    END-PERFORM

    CALL "dm_data_frame_new" USING DM-DATA-FRAME-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-DATA-FRAME-NEW-RESULT TO DF
    MOVE N-STUDENTS-TOTAL TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT
    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > N-STUDENTS-TOTAL
        MOVE SCHOOL-COL(I) TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(I)
    END-PERFORM
    MOVE "school" TO COLUMN-NAME
    PERFORM ADD-COLUMN
    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > N-STUDENTS-TOTAL
        MOVE STUDY-HOURS-COL(I) TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(I)
    END-PERFORM
    MOVE "study_hours" TO COLUMN-NAME
    PERFORM ADD-COLUMN
    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > N-STUDENTS-TOTAL
        MOVE SCORE-COL(I) TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(I)
    END-PERFORM
    MOVE "score" TO COLUMN-NAME
    PERFORM ADD-COLUMN

    MOVE DF TO DM-LMM-NEW-DATA
    MOVE "score ~ study_hours + (1 + study_hours | school)" TO DM-LMM-NEW-FORMULA
    CALL "dm_lmm_new" USING DM-LMM-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-LMM-NEW-RESULT TO MODEL
    MOVE MODEL TO DM-LMM-PRINT-SUMMARY-SELF
    CALL "dm_lmm_print_summary" USING DM-LMM-PRINT-SUMMARY DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK

    DISPLAY " "
    DISPLAY "True generating values: intercept=" TRUE-INTERCEPT ", slope=" TRUE-SLOPE
        ", random-intercept SD=6.0, random-slope SD=1.2, residual SD=4.0"

    DISPLAY " "
    DISPLAY "--- Best Linear Unbiased Predictors (BLUPs) for a few schools ---"
    MOVE MODEL TO DM-LMM-GROUP-LABELS-SELF
    CALL "dm_lmm_group_labels" USING DM-LMM-GROUP-LABELS DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-LMM-GROUP-LABELS-RESULT TO GROUP-LABELS
    PERFORM VARYING GROUP-INDEX FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL GROUP-INDEX > 2
        MOVE GROUP-LABELS TO DM-VECTOR-STRING-SELF
        COMPUTE DM-VECTOR-STRING-INDEX = GROUP-INDEX + 1
        CALL "dm_vector_string_get" USING DM-VECTOR-STRING DM-STATUS
        PERFORM CHECK
        MOVE MODEL TO DM-LMM-RANDOM-EFFECTS-FOR-GROUP-SELF
        MOVE GROUP-INDEX TO DM-LMM-RANDOM-EFFECTS-FOR-GROUP-GROUP-INDEX
        CALL "dm_lmm_random_effects_for_group" USING DM-LMM-RANDOM-EFFECTS-FOR-GROUP DM-STATUS
        PERFORM CHECK
        MOVE DM-LMM-RANDOM-EFFECTS-FOR-GROUP-RESULT TO RANDOM-EFFECTS
        MOVE RANDOM-EFFECTS TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-SELF
        MOVE 1 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-INDEX
        CALL "dm_vector_double_get" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
        PERFORM CHECK
        MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-VALUE TO INTERCEPT-SHIFT
        MOVE 2 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-INDEX
        CALL "dm_vector_double_get" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
        PERFORM CHECK
        MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-VALUE TO SLOPE-SHIFT
        DISPLAY "school " DM-VECTOR-STRING-VALUE(1:DM-VECTOR-STRING-VALUE-LENGTH)
            ": intercept shift=" INTERCEPT-SHIFT ", slope shift=" SLOPE-SHIFT
        MOVE RANDOM-EFFECTS TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
        CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    END-PERFORM
    MOVE GROUP-LABELS TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS

    DISPLAY " "
    DISPLAY "--- Prediction: population-level vs. school-adjusted ---"
    *> study_hours alone: fixed effects only.
    CALL "dm_data_frame_new" USING DM-DATA-FRAME-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-DATA-FRAME-NEW-RESULT TO NEWDATA
    PERFORM ADD-STUDY-HOURS
    PERFORM PREDICT-FIRST
    DISPLAY "5 study hours, unseen school:      " DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-VALUE " (fixed effects only)"
    *> Adding school 0 brings in that school's BLUP.
    MOVE 1 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT
    MOVE 0.0 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1)
    MOVE NEWDATA TO DF
    MOVE "school" TO COLUMN-NAME
    PERFORM ADD-COLUMN
    PERFORM PREDICT-FIRST
    DISPLAY "5 study hours, school 0 (known):    " DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-VALUE
        " (fixed effects + school 0's BLUP)"

    MOVE NEWDATA TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE MODEL TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE SPECIES-MODEL TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE PENGUINS TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    STOP RUN.

*> Adds study_hours = 5.0 to NEWDATA.
ADD-STUDY-HOURS.
    MOVE 1 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT
    MOVE 5.0 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1)
    MOVE NEWDATA TO DF
    MOVE "study_hours" TO COLUMN-NAME
    PERFORM ADD-COLUMN.

*> DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-VALUE gets MODEL's first prediction for NEWDATA.
PREDICT-FIRST.
    MOVE MODEL TO DM-LMM-PREDICT-SELF
    MOVE NEWDATA TO DM-LMM-PREDICT-NEWDATA
    CALL "dm_lmm_predict" USING DM-LMM-PREDICT DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-LMM-PREDICT-RESULT TO PREDICTION
    MOVE PREDICTION TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-SELF
    MOVE 1 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-INDEX
    CALL "dm_vector_double_get" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE PREDICTION TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS.

*> Adds the VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE items as column COLUMN-NAME of DF.
ADD-COLUMN.
    CALL "dm_vector_double_from_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DF TO DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN-SELF
    MOVE COLUMN-NAME TO DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN-COLUMN-NAME
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF TO DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN-VALUES
    CALL "dm_data_frame_add_numeric_column" USING DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS.

*> GAUSS-VALUE gets a standard normal draw (Box-Muller).
GAUSS.
    MOVE FUNCTION RANDOM TO U1
    MOVE FUNCTION RANDOM TO U2
    COMPUTE GAUSS-VALUE = FUNCTION SQRT(-2.0 * FUNCTION LOG(U1))
        * FUNCTION COS(2.0 * FUNCTION PI * U2).

*> Stops with the error after a failed call.
CHECK.
    IF NOT DM-STATUS-OK
        DISPLAY "datamunge error (" FUNCTION TRIM(DM-STATUS-KIND) "): "
            DM-STATUS-MESSAGE(1:DM-STATUS-LENGTH) UPON SYSERR
        STOP RUN RETURNING 1
    END-IF.
